abstract: >
  ROS2 Map Editor is an open-source, purely client-side (HTML5 Canvas + JavaScript) web application
  for post-processing SLAM-generated occupancy grid maps. It provides semantic-value-aware raster
  editing, an 8-neighbourhood class-aware majority-vote noise filter, a Nav2-inspired costmap
  inflation preview via multi-source distance transform, an inflation-aware A* path planning preview,
  and a 2-D ICP routine for automatic multi-session map alignment. No ROS installation, server
  backend, or build step is required.
